From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: llama: device KQ masks from per-sequence cell lists

With batched serving (unified KV, causal attention):

- KV positions, sequence-membership words and query (pos, seq) pairs are
  uploaded and the mask is built on the device instead of filling an
  [n_kv, n_tokens] host mask.
- With flash attention, the KV cells keep per-sequence cell lists and only
  those are uploaded; the attention kernel selects the cells, bounded by the
  longest sequence's KV length. A prompt prefix copied to many sequences is
  listed once per sequence, so the list tensor is sized from the cells summed
  over sequences, padded to 64Ki entries, and graph reuse checks that it still
  fits. The mask also carries the query rows per sequence of the ubatch
  (op param 2, rounded up), from which the sparse kernel picks its tile shape;
  it is part of the graph reuse key.
- llama_kv_cells tracks used cells and per-sequence positions without full
  scans, and removes a whole sequence (a finished request) in one walk over
  its position set, with the same cell states and head as removing it cell by
  cell.

Upstream: not planned in this form.

